# MyAnimeList data source (optional — AniList works without any config).
# Create an application at https://myanimelist.net/apiconfig and paste the
# client id below. (MAL's form may still ask for a callback URL — enter your
# dev origin, e.g. http://localhost:5173/ — it is NOT used: this app never
# redirects to a MyAnimeList login.)
#
# The app authenticates itself with the X-MAL-CLIENT-ID header built from
# VITE_MAL_CLIENT_ID on every API call. There is no token flow: MAL rejects
# grant_type=client_credentials. Users never connect or log in; public lists
# are read through the same-origin proxy in vite.config.ts (MAL's API has no
# CORS support).
#
# VITE_MAL_CLIENT_SECRET is optional — unused by the app (kept for apiconfig
# and the grant check in scripts/probe-mal.ts).
#
# NOTE: VITE_-prefixed values are embedded in the production JS bundle by
# design — this is a pure SPA with no backend. The client id only identifies
# the app; it grants access to no one's private data (private lists stay private).
VITE_MAL_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_MAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
